# Where this installation of freeCAM sits, and what it may charge.
#
# Copy to site.env at the repository root and edit.  site.env is not
# committed; this example is.  Both readers use it:
#
#   Python   freecam.site.setting("FREECAM_ACCOUNT")
#   bash     source validation/jobs/common.sh
#
# so keep it to plain KEY=value assignments -- no functions, no conditionals.
# $VAR and ${VAR:-default} are expanded by both.  Anything set in the
# environment wins over this file.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The PBS allocation every job from this checkout is charged to.  There is no
# default: a wrong guess spends someone else's core-hours.
FREECAM_ACCOUNT=

# --- normally derived; set only to override ---------------------------------

# Run directories and generated data.  Defaults to $SCRATCH, then
# /glade/derecho/scratch/$USER.
#FREECAM_SCRATCH=${SCRATCH:-/glade/derecho/scratch/$USER}

# The configured CESM cases.  Defaults to <repository>/../CESM_cases.
#FREECAM_CASES=/glade/work/$USER/CESM_cases

# The reference case and the oracle run it produced.  These supply the
# machine environment (.env_mach_specific.sh), atm_in, and the initial state
# every isolated run directory is copied from.  Defaults are
# $FREECAM_CASES/<case name> and $FREECAM_SCRATCH/pyCAM/PI-cam/<case name>/run
# for the case name in configs/pi_cam_icesm131.yaml.
#FREECAM_REFERENCE_CASE=
#FREECAM_REFERENCE_RUN=

# PBS queue for interactive sessions.  develop routes to cpudev, which allows
# one allocation per user.
#FREECAM_QUEUE=develop

# The online CESM surface components and coupler, which the default case runs
# live, and the completed CESM run the provider seeds them from.  Both default
# to this checkout's own build and $FREECAM_SCRATCH.
#FREECAM_CESM_PROVIDER_LIBRARY=/glade/work/<owner>/freeCAM/build/cesm/pi_atm/production-components/libpycesm_external_atm.so
#FREECAM_CESM_PROVIDER_SEED=/glade/derecho/scratch/<owner>/pyCESM/PI-atm/oracle-1month/run

# An existing native image to run against.  It is compiled in place by the
# build jobs and its manifest records absolute paths, so a checkout that has
# not built one points at another's rather than copying it.
#FREECAM_NATIVE_MANIFEST=/glade/work/<owner>/freeCAM/build/pi_cam_promoted/native_cam_manifest.json

# A trained kernel surrogate and the anchors it was fitted on.  Unset, the most
# recent validation/jobs/pi_cam_mmacro_dataset_build.pbs run under
# $FREECAM_SCRATCH is used.
#FREECAM_SURROGATE=/glade/derecho/scratch/<owner>/pyCAM/PI-cam/mmacro-dataset-<jobid>

# Published capture bundles: every argument of every call a kernel received
# over a 512-rank run, which the training notebook draws real columns from.
# Without this, only captures under $FREECAM_SCRATCH are found.
#FREECAM_CAPTURE=/glade/work/<owner>/freecam-shared

# --- using someone else's installation --------------------------------------
#
# The native image under build/ is built in place and its manifest records
# absolute paths, so it cannot be copied.  To run against an existing build
# without repeating the multi-hour build, point at the owner's checkout and
# keep your own allocation and scratch:
#
#   FREECAM_ACCOUNT=<your project>
#   FREECAM_REFERENCE_CASE=/glade/work/<owner>/CESM_cases/f.e13.F1850C5.ne16_g16.icesm131_ihesp.PI-cam-oracle.50step
#   FREECAM_REFERENCE_RUN=/glade/derecho/scratch/<owner>/pyCAM/PI-cam/f.e13.F1850C5.ne16_g16.icesm131_ihesp.PI-cam-oracle.50step/run
#   FREECAM_CESM_PROVIDER_LIBRARY=/glade/work/<owner>/freeCAM/build/cesm/pi_atm/production-components/libpycesm_external_atm.so
#   FREECAM_CESM_PROVIDER_SEED=/glade/derecho/scratch/<owner>/pyCESM/PI-atm/oracle-1month/run
#
# and run from the owner's checkout (repo=...), which needs to be readable
# but not writable: run directories are created under your own scratch.
